      "problem": "Calculate the value of $-\\frac{1}{9}-\\frac{1}{6}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We write $-\\frac{1}{9}$ as $-\\frac{2}{18}$ and $\\frac{1}{6}$ as $\\frac{3}{18},$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{2}{18}-\\frac{3}{18}=\\frac{-2-3}{18}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $-2-3$ using a number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14148354/assets/f1d24c5635fd9b7523667eb492fe3d88adf1e485b2972e1ba61e3b3d0fb212c5.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2-3}{18}=\\frac{-5}{18}=-\\frac{5}{18}.\n$$",
